commit 7d10031ebcf450174f036b0403cab1a5b5a3e1ab

C03: the processes file carries the request's own description and the final names the file (FILES1709)

In FILES1707 the projected header was a fixed Spanish phrase, so the CPU variant («consumen») and the English variant could not ground the write, and the literal's final listed the processes without saying the file was created. The header now repeats the request's own description of the listing («los 3 procesos que más CPU consumen», «the 5 processes using the most memory»), the default file name is built from the request's noun and resource word (procesos-memoria.txt, procesos-cpu.txt, processes-memory.txt), the composer is told to say it created that file with the listed processes, and a veto (missing_written_file) rejects a final that does not name the written file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


